I think the end game requires much different strategy from the rest of
the game.  I've found it useful to start a game in wizard mode
(nethack -uwizard -D) and #wish up a typical ascension kit (or usually
less, so I can see what it might be like) and the Amulet of Yendor,
and give it a try.  When the only bit of practice you get for the
endgame is when it really counts, it can be really hard.  Maybe that's
not really kosher to suggest, but I think the practice of having done
it a few times with a mocked up character gives you a lot more
perspective for when you're really doing it.

> I recall having a lot of trouble finding the portals the last time I did
> this, particularly on the plane of water. I know there is some trick with a
> scroll of gold detection, or something, which shows the portal. How does
> this work, exactly?

Cursed scrolls, non-cursed scrolls while confused, crystal balls, or
wands of secret door detection are good.  The most ideal is to use
non-cursed scrolls while confused, especially if you can confuse
yourself with a spell (your list didn't show it, by I assume you have
some spells that confuse you if you cast it?).

> Also, what is the best way to keep the Riders away from me long enough to
> stop them from killing me this time? Confused scroll of create monster and
> then tame all the acid blobs? Any other ideas?

Wands of death.  (Except for Death).  I used to like fighting Death
first, because Famine and Pestilence's attacks were pretty
frightening.  With wands of death, they're no sweat.  With so few
hitpoints, you'd be best to avoid Death because of his max-hp reducing
attack.

Zap the Riders when there are monsters between you and them and try to
take them out before they can engage you in melee combat.  Don't waste
your time killing other monsters which will allow them to revive. 
Your goal on the astral plane should be to get to the altar (any
altar!) as fast as possible.  The longer you wait, the more monsters
will get created, and the more times you'll have to fight the Riders. 
If you get to an altar that you cannot use and get back to the middle
section, confused scrolls of create monster are a good strategy to
block the Riders from getting to you.

