I can definitely understand all of those except for c.  As long as
you're aware of cockatrice corpses and always carry lizard corpses
they shouldn't be that big of an issue (though I can understand the
frustration!).  If you kill one in a big horde, try to step on it so
that nobody else can pick it up.  Or, if you can't and you see
somebody pick it up, immediately kill that monster or teleport it away
so it can't keep hitting you.  Not many monsters are generated with
gloves or are stone-resistant, so you can be (pretty) sure which
monsters will pick it up or not.

By not genociding them, a wish for a cockatrice corpse on the Astral
plane could make your life a breeze.  You can hit just about
everything but the Riders with it.  A wand of death will take care of
all of the other Riders but Death.

> I was almost killed many times on the plane of Air last time, because of the
> air elementals. What equipment should I have, or improvements should I make
> to make this less risky?

Wands of teleport are what I use.  My strategy for the plane of Air
(and the Astral one) is to find the portal and make a beeline for it,
teleporting anything out of the way that I can.  Don't get surrounded.
 Use potions to heal yourself, rather than hang around to kill
enemies.

I tend to save all of my wands of teleport in the game when they get
to (0:1).  That way, when I get to the planes, I can apply them,
thereby teleporting everything around me away.  It helps in a pinch if
you have a (small) horde surrounding you.  Much better than the
singular remaining charge would have done you (in general).

